#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:1
msgid "Verifying Build Reproducibility"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:3
msgid ""
"You can use Nix's `diff-hook` setting to compare build results. Note that "
"this hook is only executed if the results differ; it is not used for "
"determining if the results are the same."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:7
msgid ""
"For purposes of demonstration, we'll use the following Nix file, "
"`deterministic.nix` for testing:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:10
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"let\n"
"  inherit (import <nixpkgs> {}) runCommand;\n"
"in {\n"
"  stable = runCommand \"stable\" {} ''\n"
"    touch $out\n"
"  '';\n"
"\n"
"  unstable = runCommand \"unstable\" {} ''\n"
"    echo $RANDOM > $out\n"
"  '';\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:24
msgid "Additionally, `nix.conf` contains:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:29
msgid "where `/etc/nix/my-diff-hook` is an executable file containing:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:32
msgid "#!/bin/sh\n"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:34
msgid "\"For derivation $3:\""
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:35
msgid "\"$1\" \"$2\""
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:38
msgid ""
"The diff hook is executed by the same user and group who ran the build. "
"However, the diff hook does not have write access to the store path just "
"built."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:42
msgid "Spot-Checking Build Determinism"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:44
msgid ""
"Verify a path which already exists in the Nix store by passing `--check` to "
"the build command."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:47
msgid ""
"If the build passes and is deterministic, Nix will exit with a status code "
"of 0:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:62
msgid ""
"If the build is not deterministic, Nix will exit with a status code of 1:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:78
msgid "In the Nix daemon's log, we will now see:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:88
msgid ""
"Using `--check` with `--keep-failed` will cause Nix to keep the second "
"build's output in a special, `.check` path:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:100
msgid ""
"In particular, notice the `/nix/store/krpqk0l9ib0ibi1d2w52z293zw455cap-"
"unstable.check` output. Nix has copied the build results to that directory "
"where you can examine it."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:104
msgid "\\[\\]{#check-dirs-are-unregistered} **Note**"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:106
msgid ""
"Check paths are not protected against garbage collection, and this path will "
"be deleted on the next garbage collection."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:109
msgid ""
"The path is guaranteed to be alive for the duration of the `diff-hook`'s "
"execution, but may be deleted any time after."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:112
msgid ""
"If the comparison is performed as part of automated tooling, please use the "
"diff-hook or author your tooling to handle the case where the build was not "
"deterministic and also a check path does not exist."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:116
msgid ""
"`--check` is only usable if the derivation has been built on the system "
"already. If the derivation has not been built Nix will fail with the error:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/diff-hook.md:123
msgid "Run the build without `--check`, and then try with `--check` again."
msgstr ""
